---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Ask GovAI — a measured RAG over federal AI contracts"
  description="Retrieval-augmented Q&A over 670+ federal AI/ML contract awards: a structured query router + BM25 retrieval feeding grounded, cited LLM synthesis — with a reproducible eval (recall@8 = 92%; 69% BM25 baseline). Try the retrieval live in your browser."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Ask GovAI</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A small, dependency-free <strong>RAG pipeline</strong> over this site's dataset — built to be
      <em>measured, honest, and cheap</em>, not a demo. A structured query router + BM25 retrieval
      (key-free) feed grounded LLM synthesis that cites award IDs and refuses to invent.
      The retrieval below runs <strong>entirely in your browser</strong> — same algorithm as the repo, no API key, no server.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" style="padding:28px; margin-bottom:24px;">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Try the retrieval — live</h2>
    <form id="ask-form" style="display:flex; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <input
        id="ask-q"
        type="text"
        aria-label="Ask a question about federal AI/ML contracts"
        placeholder='e.g. "which vendors hold the largest AI contracts at the DoD?"'
        style="flex:1 1 340px; background:var(--bg); color:var(--text); border:1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius:4px; padding:12px 14px; font-size:15px;"
      />
      <button type="submit" class="btn" style="padding:12px 22px;">Retrieve</button>
    </form>
    <p id="ask-status" role="status" style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); margin:10px 0 0;">
      Loads the full 670+-contract dataset (~650&nbsp;KB) on first search, then everything runs locally.
    </p>
    <div id="ask-strategy" aria-live="polite" style="display:none; font-family:monospace; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:14px;"></div>
    <ol id="ask-results" role="list" style="list-style:none; padding:0; margin:10px 0 0;"></ol>
    <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:14px;">
      This page demonstrates the <strong>retrieval</strong> half. The grounded, cited <strong>synthesis</strong> half
      runs in the repo CLI with a free Gemini key or a Claude key —
      <a href="https://github.com/Nandanhegde1/govai-contracts/tree/main/ask" rel="noopener" target="_blank">run it yourself</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="detail-grid">
    <section class="card" style="padding:28px;">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">How it works</h2>
      <pre style="font-size:12.5px; overflow-x:auto; line-height:1.5;">question ─▶ query router ─▶ structured path
               │              (superlative / NAICS →
               ▼               filter + sort by amount)
        BM25 retrieval ─▶ top-k contracts
        (key-free, offline)     │
                       grounded LLM synthesis ─▶ cited answer
                       (cite award_ids, refuse
                        if unsupported)</pre>
      <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted);">
        The cost decision: <strong>don't pay a model to find documents a ranking function can find.</strong>
        BM25 handles topical lookup for free; the router handles what lexical ranking <em>cannot</em> do by
        construction (superlatives, explicit NAICS codes) by answering structurally against the data.
        The LLM does only the one thing it's uniquely good at — synthesizing a grounded answer from the
        retrieved records. Synthesis is provider-agnostic: free Gemini or paid Claude.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card" style="padding:28px;">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">The eval — measure, diagnose, fix</h2>
      <table style="width:100%; font-size:13.5px; border-collapse:collapse;">
        <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-strong);"><th style="text-align:left; padding:6px 4px;">Metric</th><th style="text-align:left; padding:6px 4px;">Result</th></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:6px 4px;"><strong>Retrieval recall@8 (routed)</strong></td><td style="padding:6px 4px;"><strong>92% (12/13)</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:6px 4px;">Retrieval recall@8 (BM25 baseline)</td><td style="padding:6px 4px;">69% (9/13)</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:6px 4px;">Answer accuracy / latency / cost</td><td style="padding:6px 4px;">printed by <code>ask:eval</code> with a key</td></tr>
      </table>
      <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:12px;">
        The baseline measured <strong>69%</strong>. The misses were diagnosed, not hidden: superlative
        queries ("largest contract…") and explicit NAICS codes are structurally unanswerable by term
        overlap — so a thin router now answers those against the data (a general mechanism, gold set
        frozen before it was built), taking recall to <strong>92%</strong>. The one remaining miss is a
        semantic-disambiguation limit of lexical retrieval — that's the honest residual, and the
        roadmap (dense embeddings) targets exactly it.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size:14px;">
        <a href="https://github.com/Nandanhegde1/govai-contracts/blob/main/ask/README.md" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Full eval write-up →</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="card" style="padding:28px; margin-top:24px;">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Run it yourself</h2>
    <pre style="font-size:13px; overflow-x:auto;">git clone https://github.com/Nandanhegde1/govai-contracts && cd govai-contracts && npm install

npm run ask -- "which vendors won the biggest DoD AI contracts?"   # retrieval — no key needed
GEMINI_API_KEY=... npm run ask -- "who supports the DoD JAIC?"     # grounded, cited answer (free key)
npm run ask:eval                                                    # reproduce the eval</pre>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  // The same retrieval pipeline as ask/retrieve.ts, ported to the browser:
  // BM25 (k1=1.5, b=0.75) + the structured query router. No key, no server.
  type C = {
    id: string; award_id: string; recipient: string; amount: number; agency: string;
    sub_agency?: string; description: string; naics_code?: string; naics_desc?: string;
    psc_desc?: string; pop_state?: string; matched_keywords?: string[];
  };

  const STOP = new Set(('the a an and or of to for in on with by is are be this that it as at from into ' +
    'shall will contractor support services service contract award task order').split(' '));
  const stem = (t: string) =>
    t.length > 4 && t.endsWith('ies') ? t.slice(0, -3) + 'y'
    : t.length > 4 && t.endsWith('es') ? t.slice(0, -2)
    : t.length > 3 && t.endsWith('s') ? t.slice(0, -1) : t;
  const tokenize = (s: string) => (s.toLowerCase().match(/[a-z0-9]+/g) ?? []).filter(t => t.length >= 2 && !STOP.has(t)).map(stem);
  const docText = (c: C) => [c.description, c.recipient, c.agency, c.sub_agency, c.naics_desc, c.psc_desc, c.pop_state, (c.matched_keywords ?? []).join(' ')].filter(Boolean).join(' ');

  let docs: C[] | null = null;
  let idx: { tf: Map<string, number>[]; df: Map<string, number>; len: number[]; avg: number } | null = null;

  async function load(status: HTMLElement): Promise<C[]> {
    if (docs) return docs;
    status.textContent = 'Loading dataset…';
    const raw = await fetch('/export/all.json').then(r => r.json());
    docs = (Array.isArray(raw) ? raw : raw.contracts) as C[];
    const tf: Map<string, number>[] = []; const df = new Map<string, number>(); const len: number[] = [];
    for (const d of docs) {
      const toks = tokenize(docText(d)); const m = new Map<string, number>();
      for (const t of toks) m.set(t, (m.get(t) ?? 0) + 1);
      for (const t of m.keys()) df.set(t, (df.get(t) ?? 0) + 1);
      tf.push(m); len.push(toks.length);
    }
    idx = { tf, df, len, avg: len.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / (len.length || 1) };
    status.textContent = `${docs.length} contracts indexed locally.`;
    return docs;
  }

  function bm25(query: string, k: number): { c: C; score: number }[] {
    const N = docs!.length; const q = [...new Set(tokenize(query))];
    const scored = docs!.map((c, i) => {
      let s = 0;
      for (const t of q) {
        const f = idx!.tf[i].get(t); if (!f) continue;
        const n = idx!.df.get(t) ?? 0;
        s += Math.log(1 + (N - n + 0.5) / (n + 0.5)) * (f * 2.5) / (f + 1.5 * (0.25 + 0.75 * idx!.len[i] / idx!.avg));
      }
      return { c, score: s };
    });
    return scored.filter(h => h.score > 0).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score).slice(0, k);
  }

  const ALIASES: Record<string, string> = { dod: 'department of defense', doj: 'department of justice', hhs: 'health and human services', gsa: 'general services administration', nasa: 'aeronautics and space', dhs: 'homeland security', va: 'veterans affairs' };

  function retrieveSmart(query: string, k = 8) {
    const q = query.toLowerCase();
    const naics = (q.match(/\b(\d{6})\b/) ?? [])[1];
    let agency: string | undefined;
    for (const a of new Set(docs!.map(d => d.agency))) if (q.includes(a.toLowerCase())) { agency = a.toLowerCase(); break; }
    if (!agency) for (const [al, full] of Object.entries(ALIASES)) if (new RegExp('\\b' + al + '\\b').test(q)) { agency = full; break; }
    const sup = /\b(largest|biggest|top|highest|most valuable|most expensive)\b/.test(q) ? 'desc' : /\b(smallest|lowest|cheapest)\b/.test(q) ? 'asc' : null;
    if (!naics && !sup) return { hits: bm25(query, k), strategy: 'bm25' };
    let pool = docs!; const parts: string[] = [];
    if (naics) { pool = pool.filter(c => c.naics_code === naics); parts.push('naics=' + naics); }
    if (agency) { const a = agency; pool = pool.filter(c => (c.agency + ' ' + (c.sub_agency ?? '')).toLowerCase().includes(a)); parts.push('agency~"' + a + '"'); }
    if (!pool.length) return { hits: bm25(query, k), strategy: 'bm25 (structured pool empty)' };
    const dir = sup === 'asc' ? 1 : -1;
    const structured = [...pool].sort((a, b) => dir * (a.amount - b.amount)).slice(0, Math.ceil(k / 2)).map((c, i) => ({ c, score: 100 - i }));
    parts.push('amount ' + (sup ?? 'desc'));
    const seen = new Set(structured.map(h => h.c.award_id));
    const fill = bm25(query, k).filter(h => !seen.has(h.c.award_id));
    return { hits: [...structured, ...fill].slice(0, k), strategy: 'structured(' + parts.join(', ') + ') + bm25 fill' };
  }

  const form = document.getElementById('ask-form') as HTMLFormElement;
  const input = document.getElementById('ask-q') as HTMLInputElement;
  const status = document.getElementById('ask-status') as HTMLElement;
  const stratEl = document.getElementById('ask-strategy') as HTMLElement;
  const results = document.getElementById('ask-results') as HTMLElement;
  const esc = (s: string) => s.replace(/[&<>"]/g, ch => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' }[ch] as string));

  form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const q = input.value.trim();
    if (!q) return;
    await load(status);
    const t0 = performance.now();
    const { hits, strategy } = retrieveSmart(q, 8);
    const ms = (performance.now() - t0).toFixed(1);
    stratEl.style.display = 'block';
    stratEl.textContent = `retrieval: ${strategy} · ${ms}ms · in-browser`;
    results.innerHTML = hits.length
      ? hits.map(h => `
        <li style="border:1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius:6px; padding:12px 14px; margin-top:10px;">
          <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap; font-size:13.5px;">
            <a href="/contracts/${esc(h.c.id)}/" style="font-weight:600;">[${esc(h.c.award_id)}] ${esc(h.c.recipient)}</a>
            <span style="color:var(--text-muted); white-space:nowrap;">$${Math.round(h.c.amount).toLocaleString('en-US')}</span>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size:12.5px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:4px;">${esc(h.c.agency)}${h.c.sub_agency ? ' / ' + esc(h.c.sub_agency) : ''}</div>
          <div style="font-size:13px; margin-top:6px;">${esc(h.c.description.slice(0, 220))}${h.c.description.length > 220 ? '…' : ''}</div>
        </li>`).join('')
      : '<li style="margin-top:10px; color:var(--text-muted);">No lexical matches — try vendor, agency, or mission terms.</li>';
  });
</script>
